      "id": "sol.ahsme-1982-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Set \\(t=\\log_ba,\\) so \\(a=b^t\\) and \\(p=\\frac{\\log_bt}{t}.\\) Then \\(a^p=(b^t)^{\\frac{\\log_bt}{t}},\\) which equals \\(b^{\\log_bt}=t.\\) Therefore \\(a^p=\\log_ba.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
